.TH "RTCERROREVENT" "3JS" "August 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCErrorEvent \- RTCErrorEvent
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]RTCErrorEvent\f[B]\f[R] interface of the WebRTC API
represents an error event sent to a WebRTC object.
It inherits from the standard \f[CR]Event\f[R] interface, adding
RTC\-specific information describing the error.
.PP
The \f[CR]error\f[R] events fired at \f[CR]RTCDataChannel\f[R] and
\f[CR]RTCDtlsTransport\f[R] are instances of this object.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] WebRTC defines other error event interfaces, such as
\f[CR]RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent\f[R], which are used for errors
that have other special information sharing requirements.
.RE
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
\f[B]RTCErrorEvent()\f[R]
Creates and returns a new \f[CR]RTCErrorEvent\f[R] object.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Also inherits properties from its parent interface,
\f[CI]Event\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]error\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
An \f[CR]RTCError\f[R] object specifying RTC\-specific information about
the error.
This includes information such as the error type and cause, and the
location that triggered the error.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Only inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]Event\f[I].\f[R]
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
